    "updated_at": "2021-02-26T18:03:53Z",
    "body": "I think this feature could also directly solve the \"how do I declaratively [share inline styles](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/831#issuecomment-584801621) between components\"? e.g.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<template id=myStyle>\r\n  <style>\r\n    .foo { display: inline }\r\n  </style>\r\n</template>\r\n\r\n<my-custom-element id=ce1>\r\n  <template shadowroot=open>\r\n    <style clone=#myStyle></style>\r\n    /* other stuff that goes in the shadow tree. Not the same as #ce2 because its data model differs  */\r\n  </template>\r\n<my-custom-element>\r\n    \r\n<my-custom-element id=ce2>\r\n  <template shadowroot=open>\r\n    <style clone=#myStyle></style>\r\n    /* other stuff that goes in the shadow tree. Not the same as #ce1 because its data model differs */\r\n  </template>\r\n<my-custom-element>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere is a slight hiccup in the above since the myStyle reference within the custom elements is within a different tree scope. But there should be a way to fix that somehow.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
